The present invention provides a system and method for smoothing photovoltaic power generation. Photovoltaic power plants have the inherent problem of generation intermittency caused by the variation in weather conditions over a period of seconds, minutes, and hours. This intermittency results in a variability of active power injection into the electrical grid by the photovoltaic power plant.
1. A system for smoothing photovoltaic generation intermittency characterized in that it comprises secondary converter (1), battery bank (2), photovoltaic array (3), primary converter (4), instrumentation system (5), microcontroller (6), drivers (7), external electrical network or grid (8) and measurements (9).
12. A method for smoothing photovoltaic generation intermittency characterized in that it comprises:
1. secondary converter operating in a four-layer cascaded control;
2. the first control layer is responsible for controlling the AC currents of the secondary converter;
3. the second control layer is responsible for regulating the DC link voltage of the secondary converter;
4. the third control layer controls the battery bank current;
5. the fourth control layer is responsible for generating the reference battery bank current by considering the power ramp.

