using the estimated relative pose, projecting landmarks from the three-dimensional model of the object into a dimensional space of the received image of the instance of the object;
comparing, in the dimensional space, characteristics of corresponding of the projected landmarks and the first plurality of the detected landmarks; and
determining whether a threshold level of positional correspondence exists between positions of corresponding of the projected landmarks and the first plurality of the detected landmarks.
